{
  "_readme": [
    "THE hostile-input table for dl-router's name validation. Both suites read",
    "THIS file: tests/test_security.py drives safety.py from it and",
    "tests/sanitize.test.mjs drives extension/sanitize.js from it.",
    "",
    "It exists because the two tables used to be hand-copied literal lists in",
    "the two test files. Differential fuzzing found 991 inputs the two",
    "implementations disagreed on, none of which either list covered -- and the",
    "sidecar was the LOOSER side, so /mkdir could create a directory the",
    "extension would never route into, which is how the NFC anti-homoglyph",
    "check gets defeated.",
    "",
    "Every non-ASCII character is a backslash-u escape on purpose: this file",
    "must stay plain ASCII so it greps, diffs and reviews as text. A long",
    "repeated string is written as {\"prefix\": <str?>, \"repeat\": <str>,",
    "\"count\": <n>} and both loaders expand it to prefix + repeat*count; an",
    "object without a \"repeat\" key is passed through verbatim (that is how",
    "the non-string cases stay non-strings).",
    "",
    "Adding a case here automatically binds BOTH implementations. That is the",
    "point -- do not add a case to one test file instead."
  ],

